	quests: [
		{
			description: [
				"Observe the silhouette, entrance, nearby terrain and mob sounds before entering. Large structures often contain vertical routes, traps or sealed encounters that are invisible from the doorway."
				"Mark the entrance on the map and place a physical trail marker. Record whether the site is unexplored, active, cleared or reserved for the group."
				"The Chronicle treats structures as evidence. Loot is useful, but architecture tells you what kind of danger was expected here."
				"Dungeons and Taverns, Dungeons Plus, the Graveyard, Towns and Towers, and Repurposed Structures add destinations with different scales. Observe from outside and choose an objective before entering every doorway you see."
			]
			id: "08B4FE3DADF6D411"
			rewards: [{
				id: "146CD2EE6C640B2C"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "Pause before the front door"
			tasks: [{
				id: "7427F5993060FEC5"
				title: "I read this lesson and tried it in the world"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "A Structure Is a Signal"
			x: 0.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["08B4FE3DADF6D411"]
			description: [
				"Carry food, light, blocks, water and a way home. Then add environment-specific tools: milk for effects, fire resistance, ladders, doors, boats or slow falling."
				"Leave one inventory section empty and place valuables into a backpack before entry. Full pockets make good loot feel like a logistics problem."
				"Set a return time. Tired groups take worse risks and communicate less clearly."
				"Mark entrances, cleared routes, dangerous branches, and exits differently. Bring spare blocks and a water bucket, retreat to a secured room when inventory fills, and never let loot pressure erase the return path."
			]
			id: "14EC247DD954A406"
			rewards: [{
				id: "35AC61048A924FE3"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "Every dungeon asks the same five questions first"
			tasks: [{
