				title: "I read this lesson and tried it in the world"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Pack for the Unknown"
			x: 2.0d
			y: -2.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["08B4FE3DADF6D411"]
			description: [
				"Lootr gives each player their own chest inventory in supported structures. Let everyone open the chest rather than breaking it or assuming one person's result is all that exists."
				"Unique boss drops, decorations and items outside Lootr may still be shared. Announce them and decide ownership before leaving the room."
				"Do not dismantle containers until the group confirms everyone has looted and the structure no longer needs them."
				"Lootr gives supported containers a separate inventory for each player. Leave the container intact and let each teammate open it; breaking or moving it can discard the very multiplayer benefit the mod provides."
			]
			id: "4F7A5E294B48D343"
			rewards: [{
				id: "47813EE7B3F57E67"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "Individual chests remove races, not decisions"
			tasks: [{
				id: "3962D60C6566DF8C"
				title: "I read this lesson and tried it in the world"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Lootr and Shared Treasure"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["08B4FE3DADF6D411"]
			description: [
				"Choose a consistent marker: torches on the exit side, chalk arrows or a distinctive block. Explain the convention before the first branch."
				"Close or mark cleared dead ends and leave hazards visible enough to be understood. Random torch spam can make a route less readable."
				"Mark stairs and level changes especially carefully. Most lost teams know their coordinates but not which floor contains the exit."
				"Mark entrances, cleared routes, dangerous branches, and exits differently. Bring spare blocks and a water bucket, retreat to a secured room when inventory fills, and never let loot pressure erase the return path."
			]
			id: "4258CA348D075B32"
			rewards: [{
				id: "7FD8BE0A70C689DC"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
