			title: "The Dungeon Route Language"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 2.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["14EC247DD954A406", "4258CA348D075B32"]
			description: [
				"Mineshafts, dungeons, temples, strongholds, fortresses and monuments may be much larger than their vanilla versions. Expect alternate rooms, longer routes and environmental storytelling."
				"Old walkthroughs and remembered vanilla dimensions may be wrong. Explore the actual structure instead of digging directly toward where a room used to be."
				"Preserve useful hubs and intersections. A rebuilt stronghold or mineshaft can become infrastructure after it stops being a threat."
				"YUNG's Better Dungeons includes redesigned small dungeons plus Catacombs, Fortresses of the Undead, and Spider Caves. Read block palette, webs, vertical shafts, and repeated rooms as warnings about the encounter ahead."
			]
			id: "65E1DDB986D0FBBB"
			rewards: [{
				id: "13D8866817D14CEF"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 15
			}]
			subtitle: "Vanilla landmarks now have real internal logic"
