			}]
			title: "Lead an Expedition"
			x: 10.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"YUNG's Better Dungeons includes three major added families alongside redesigned small dungeons. Catacombs emphasise rooms and levels, Fortresses of the Undead signal sustained combat, and Spider Caves advertise webs and constrained movement."
				"Read the entrance and surrounding terrain before descending. Carry tools for webs, vertical shafts, spawners, locked sightlines, and a retreat room rather than bringing one generic cave kit to every structure."
				"Mark branches with a consistent language and clear each level methodically. A large dungeon becomes manageable when the team can state which floor, entrance, and safe room they mean."
			]
			id: "0035451CF4EC0CFE"
			rewards: [{
				id: "401BED92128D9293"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "Catacomb, undead fortress, and spider cave"
			tasks: [{
				id: "01C47B22AA49AF32"
				title: "I read this field lesson and tried its method"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Dungeon School: Recognise the YUNG Families"
			x: 0.0d
			y: 7.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["0035451CF4EC0CFE"]
			description: [
				"Mineshafts, strongholds, desert and jungle temples, ocean monuments, Nether fortresses, witch huts, the End island, bridges, and extras may preserve a vanilla purpose while changing scale and route."
				"Do not rely on memorised vanilla coordinates for portal rooms, traps, treasure, or bosses. Survey, read repeated architecture, and keep the entrance marked before using shortcuts from another version or showcase."
				"The reward is rediscovery: recognise the structure's role, then let the rebuilt layout teach the new route. Record confirmed paths for this world instead of treating a mismatch as broken generation."
			]
			id: "367294FE97FB5DAF"
			rewards: [{
				id: "421B6A6F810DDEB9"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "YUNG rebuilds the structures you thought you knew"
			tasks: [{
				id: "4BB9AF8F50A3D477"
				title: "I read this field lesson and tried its method"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Dungeon School: Familiar Name, New Layout"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 7.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["367294FE97FB5DAF"]
			description: [
				"Repurposed Structures creates variations of familiar villages, temples, outposts, fortresses, dungeons, and other landmarks in biomes where their materials and hazards change."
				"Use the structure's function plus its biome palette to identify it. A snowy, jungle, Nether, or End variant may contain recognisable logic without looking like the Overworld reference in a wiki image."
				"These structures are evidence that the world's cultures adapted creatively rather than copied a single universal template everywhere. Photograph one architectural change and preserve it in the museum or builder's yard as a usable palette lesson."
			]
			id: "3D63A9B7D6224D3A"
			rewards: [{
				id: "3C84E63BABA2502E"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "Vanilla ideas adapted to new biomes and dimensions"
			tasks: [{
