			title: "Dungeon School: Judge Landmark Scale"
			x: 0.0d
			y: 9.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7E71E1637E188F41"]
			description: [
				"A supported Lootr chest generates a personal inventory when each player opens it. The colours and appearance may change after use, but another player can still have their own unopened contents."
				"Do not break, move, funnel, or automatically extract an unfamiliar dungeon chest until the whole team has checked it. Lootr solves shared-loot conflict only while the special container remains intact."
				"Mark worthwhile sites and tell absent players what danger and unopened routes remain there. Individual treasure should reduce arguments without eliminating cooperation, rescue, or the story of exploring the structure together."
			]
			id: "19A4D61FDA9A4087"
			rewards: [{
				id: "387FBDD56B8CD1CD"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 10
			}]
			subtitle: "Every player gets a chest; everyone preserves the container"
			tasks: [{
				id: "151F0F3B120CA832"
				title: "I read this field lesson and tried its method"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Dungeon School: Lootr Etiquette"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 9.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["19A4D61FDA9A4087"]
			description: [
				"Choose one uncleared structure and prepare a role-based team: navigation, light and blocks, food and recovery, ranged control, and empty storage. Establish a named camp outside before entry."
				"During the run, mark the entrance, safe room, uncleared branches, spawners, vertical transitions, and exit. Open Lootr containers individually and stop when recovery capacity becomes more valuable than another room."
				"Return with coordinates, structure identification, cleared status, hazards, photographs, and a note about remaining objectives and useful loot sources. The report completes the expedition by turning one group's risk into the next group's knowledge."
			]
			id: "275AF8576E34B2C3"
